The “Eighteen Siddhars” are not one stable historical club. Different lists combine poets, physicians, alchemists, deities and legendary immortals.

Bogar/Boganathar — S5/E2. The globe-traveling alchemist credited with creating Palani’s sacred image from a mysterious medicinal compound and, in some traditions, journeying to China or becoming associated with Laozi.

Agastya — S5/E1. A Vedic sage transformed in Tamil tradition into the primordial physician, grammarian, alchemist and southern master whose life spans incompatible historical eras.

Tirumūlar — S5/E2. Finds a herd grieving its dead cowherd and, according to legend, transfers consciousness into the man’s body; afterward he composes one verse per year for thousands of years.

Korakkar — S5/E2. The Tamil transformation of Gorakhnath: cave yogi, physician, alchemist and traveler linked to Sri Lanka and numerous sites competing to possess his final resting place.

Konganar — S4/E2. A yogi whose pride in destructive powers is shattered when an ordinary householder woman proves spiritually stronger than he is.

Karuvūrar — S5/E3. Historical temple-linked poet or architect surrounded by later accounts of metallurgy, image consecration and impossible engineering knowledge.

