Who Initiated Abhinavagupta into the Kaula Tradition?
Opening hook

    Abhinavagupta studied philosophy, grammar, poetry, ritual, Buddhism and multiple schools of Śaivism. He sought out teacher after teacher until he became one of medieval India’s most learned men.

    Yet in his own account, scholarship did not complete him.

    The decisive transformation came from an almost unknown master named Śambhunātha—and from a woman whose name history did not preserve.

Visual sequence:

    A manuscript of the Tantrāloka.

    Abhinavagupta’s name brightly illuminated.

    The name Śambhunātha appearing once, then fading.

