Modern consciousness angle

This is one of the rare traditions where a comparison with contemporary cognitive science could be productive without forcing a simplistic equivalence.
Krama model

Experience is not a static representation. It is an unfolding sequence:

    anticipation;

    emergence;

    determination;

    appropriation;

    dissolution;

    absence;

    renewed emergence.

Predictive-processing comparison

A modern model may examine:

    prediction;

    sensory updating;

    object stabilization;

    salience;

    memory;

    model revision.

The traditions are not saying the same thing.

The valuable comparison is structural:

    Both challenge the idea that consciousness receives a finished world. What appears as a stable object is generated across temporal stages.

Krama goes further by treating the entire sequence as the self-presentation of divine consciousness.

