Misleading framings to avoid
“Nepal’s Harry Potter”

It trivializes a living priestly tradition and encourages the audience to treat local religion as fantasy entertainment.
“A Buddhist black magician”

“Black magic” is an unstable outsider category. Use:

    tantric priest;

    siddha;

    ritual specialist;

    legendary magician where discussing folklore.

“Secret tunnels prove ancient advanced technology”

No verified survey currently supports the whole legendary network.
“Jamana practised Tibetan Buddhism”

Newar Vajrayāna is historically and institutionally distinct, though it shares Sanskrit Buddhist traditions with Tibet.
“He was an Aghori”

There is no basis for importing an Indian Śaiva identity.
“The rain painting definitely contained snake blood”

Describe it as a feature of the legend.
“The film tells his true life”

The film demonstrates cultural memory and artistic reception.
“Newar priests still possess his supernatural methods”

Do not make claims on behalf of living communities or pressure practitioners to disclose restricted material.
