The Pāśupatasūtra and Kauṇḍinya’s Pañcārthabhāṣya preserve a systematic teaching organized around categories such as cause, effect, discipline, union and the end of suffering. Manuscripts were recovered and edited in the twentieth century, with the Trivandrum Sanskrit Series edition remaining a central source.

