Later Brahmanical philosophical works criticized Pāśupata accounts of God, causation and liberation, showing that the system had become a recognizable intellectual opponent rather than merely a group of wandering eccentrics. Daśgupta’s survey gives a useful older overview of the philosophical system and Kauṇḍinya’s likely period.

