Misleading framings to avoid
“Nepal’s secret underground city”

Shantipur may preserve a layered sacred interior, but a vast verified tunnel-city has not been established.
“The original Monkey Temple founder”

Śāntikara belongs to one sacred-history explanation of the monument. Archaeology and inscriptional history require separate treatment.
“An immortal Buddhist wizard”

Use:

    tantric master;

    siddha;

    Vajrācārya;

    legendary immortal presence.

“Nāga blood proves literal dragon sacrifice”

The phrase belongs to later legend and symbolic imagination unless material evidence demonstrates otherwise.
“Buddhist rain magic was primitive weather science”

It was a ritual-political ecology operating within a different understanding of agency.
“Opening the chamber would solve everything”

It might damage a sacred monument, violate community authority and still fail to answer textual-history questions.
“Śāntikara was Tibetan”

He belongs to the Newar Buddhist tradition of the Kathmandu Valley.
