A popular interpretation links the name with four limbs, especially because the prince’s limbs are restored by Gorakhnāth.

However, the etymology should not be treated as certain. The name may have existed independently before the Punjabi mutilation legend explained it retrospectively.
Sahaj Nāth

Some descendant or community traditions worship Puran as Bāwā Sahaj Nāth.

