Modern literary transformation: Lūṇā
Why it deserves a major section

Batalvi’s retelling turns the original legend inside out.

Traditional moral structure:

    Puran = pure;

    Lūṇā = desire and deception;

    king = tragically misled;

    Gorakhnāth = salvation.

Modern structure:

    Lūṇā = young woman trapped by caste and marriage;

    king = beneficiary of structural power;

    Puran = morally pure but also privileged;

    society = producer of the catastrophe.

