Safest

    Met Open Access Aurangzeb images;

    custom maps;

    custom mercury animation;

    public-domain Mughal artwork where the scan is explicitly open;

    original document diagrams;

    your own Jakhbar footage;

    brief translated excerpts;

    interviews released for commercial use.

Verify individually

    the 1967 book’s plates;

    Archive.org scans;

    British Museum images;

    Persian document photographs;

    newspaper images;

    modern translations;

    lecture footage;

    manuscripts from libraries;

    images from community archives.

Safety and cultural cautions

Do not:

    give mercury-purification instructions;

    suggest ingesting or handling mercury;

    reproduce historical medicinal formulations as usable recipes;

    imply that “natural” or “alchemical” mercury is safe;

    turn the video into contemporary Hindu–Muslim incitement;

    use one document to erase documented violence elsewhere;

    call Ānand Nāth a fraud or Aurangzeb a convert without evidence;

    handle old documents without archival supervision.

